  "query_preview": "..\n\nToday through Sunday...\n\nWesterly flow to mild ridging will dominate through mid week,\nkeeping conditions mostly warm and dry. Today, a tight surface\npressure gradient and low level jet across southeast MT ahead of \na weak cold front will create breezy conditions through the day. \nSoutheast wind gusts of 30-45 mph are expected. As far as the weak\ncold front, not much is expected in the way of winds or \nsignificant temperature changes. As an upper level low works its \nway onto the west coast mid week, a slight southwesterly flow over\nsouthwest MT will promote small precipitation chances (10-30%) \nover the Absaroka-Beartooths Tuesday-Thursday. Towards Friday, \nensembles generally show that low moving up into the region. \nThere's still uncertainty at this time regarding the track of this\nsystem which will affect precipitation amounts, mountain snow \nimpacts, and wind potential. TS",
